C# Windows Forms – File Handling System

1. Project Overview

This project is a C# Windows Forms application developed using Visual Studio. It demonstrates basic file handling operations, including adding items to a ListBox, deleting items, deleting files, writing text to files, and reading files from the computer.

2. Technologies Used

- C#
- .NET Windows Forms
- Visual Studio
- System.IO
- StreamReader
- OpenFileDialog
- SaveFileDialog

3. Features

Add Item

Allows users to enter text and add it to the ListBox.

Delete Item

Removes the selected item from the ListBox.

Delete File

Allows users to select a file from their computer and delete it after confirmation.

Write All Text

Saves all items displayed in the ListBox into a text file selected by the user.

Stream Reader

Allows users to select and read a text file. Each line of the file is displayed as an item in the ListBox.

4. How to Run the Project

1. Open Visual Studio.
2. Open the C# Windows Forms project.
3. Make sure all required controls are available on Form1.
4. Build the project to check for errors.
5. Run the application.
6. Use the buttons to perform file handling operations.

5. How to Use the Application

1. Enter text in the TextBox and click Add Item.
2. Select an item in the ListBox and click Delete Item.
3. Click Write All Text to save the ListBox contents to a file.
4. Click Stream Reader to select and read a file.
5. Click Delete File to select a file and delete it after confirmation.

6. File Storage

The application allows users to select files from the Desktop or other accessible folders on their computer.

The Save File dialog allows users to choose the file name and location for saving text.

7. Important Notes

- The application must have permission to access the selected file.
- Deleting a file may permanently remove it.
- Write All Text replaces the existing contents of the selected destination file.
- Stream Reader is intended for reading text-based files.
- Always verify the selected file before deleting or overwriting it.

8. Learning Objectives

This project helps students understand:

- Windows Forms event handling.
- Working with TextBox and ListBox controls.
- Reading files using StreamReader.
- Writing files using File.WriteAllText.
- Deleting files using File.Delete.
- Selecting files using OpenFileDialog.
- Saving files using SaveFileDialog.

9. Conclusion

The File Handling System demonstrates how a C# Windows Forms application can manage text and files using built-in .NET classes. It provides practical experience with user interface controls, file operations, and event-driven programming.